{"name":"Overgrown Trellis","hex":"#6a8988","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"overgrown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having large numbers of plants which have become too big, and are hence spoiling the picturesqueness of a garden.","Having grown bigger without developing maturity or changing character."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of overgrow"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/overgrown"},{"term":"trellis","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor garden frame that can be used for partitioning a common area.","An outdoor garden frame that can be used to grow vines or other climbing plants."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To train or arrange (plants) so that they grow against a trellis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trellis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Overgrown","blocks":[{"text":"Overgrown is the second studio album by English singer-songwriter James Blake. It was released on 5 April 2013 by Blake's Atlas Records, along with Republic Records and Polydor Records. The album features guest appearances from Wu-Tang Clan member RZA and English musician Brian Eno. Overgrown debuted at number eight on the UK Albums Chart and at number one on the US Dance/Electronic chart. It was supported by lead single \"Retrograde\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/de/James_Blake_-_Overgrown_album_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overgrown","wikidata":"Q7113670"},{"title":"Trellis","blocks":[{"text":"A trellis is an architectural structure, usually made from an open framework or lattice of interwoven or intersecting pieces of wood, bamboo, or metal that is normally made to support and display climbing plants, especially shrubs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Wernberg_Klosterweg_2_ehem._Schloss_Arkadenhof_Brunnentrog_um_15